  "result": "I implemented `slugify` in `src/strings.js` and added 12 tests to `test/strings.test.js`. `npm test` passes all 14 tests, including the 2 that were already there.\n\nHow it works:\n1. Lowercase the text, which also turns `Đ` into `đ`.\n2. Split accented letters into a base letter plus accent marks, then drop the marks. This handles Vietnamese and most other accented Latin letters (`é`, `ç`, `ü`, …).\n3. Swap the few Latin letters that step 2 can't split, using a small lookup table. `đ` becomes `d`, as you asked. I also added `ł`→`l`, `ø`→`o`, `ß`→`ss`, `æ`→`ae` and `œ`→`oe`, which would otherwise turn into hyphens.\n4. Replace each run of characters other than `a-z` and `0-9` with a single hyphen, and trim hyphens from both ends.\n5. Cut to 50 characters, then remove any hyphens left at the end by the cut.\n\nThe tests cover each rule, including a case where character 50 is a hyphen, so the result comes out at 49 characters. Input that is all punctuation, or empty, gives an empty string.\n\n`slugify` will throw if it's given something that isn't a string, such as `null`.",
